Exercise 2.3 — Rule → SQL
Translate these marketing expectations into SQL (against customers in dq_learning):
1.  Every customer must have a non-NULL email.
2.  Every email must be well-formed (contains @, a domain, and a TLD).
3.  No two customers may share an email.
Answer:
-- Rule 1
SELECT customer_id, 
    first_name, 
    last_name, 
    email, 
    is_active
FROM customers
WHERE email IS NULL
OR email = '' 
;
-- Rule 2  
SELECT customer_id,
    first_name,
    last_name,
    email,
    is_active
FROM customers
WHERE email NOT REGEXP '^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$'
;
-- Rule 3  
SELECT email,
    COUNT(*) AS `count`
FROM customers
GROUP BY email
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
AND email IS NOT NULL
;
